    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d931">

                <pb facs="1051" n="947" xml:id="pg947"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00 Revolutions/330: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Burdett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-11T19:00:00-04:00">July 11, 1932—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Your 100, July 9, 4 p.m. Department understands from Navy Department that
                    Chief of the Naval Mission advised the Peruvian authorities that their request
                    should be transmitted through the Peruvian Embassy in Washington. Department
                    therefore will not take any action unless and until the matter is taken up by
                    the Peruvian Embassy here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
